{
  "title": "Linux Fundamentals: From the Shell to System Administration",
  "description": "A hands-on introduction to Linux for developers and IT beginners. You will learn how a Linux system is put together, how to work efficiently in the shell, how files, users and permissions work (including the octal arithmetic behind chmod and umask), how to process text with grep, sed and awk, and how to write shell scripts that behave well when things go wrong. You will then manage processes and services with systemd, schedule jobs, handle packages, disks and networking, and finish by building an automated, rotating backup run by a systemd timer. Every script in the course comes as a sample file you can run.",
